#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:5
#: f0d1afe655fd40cd9706935a3f1d7b81
msgid "KDE CAN ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:9
#: e084eff6ed4d447ebc39b670884985fa
msgid "KDECAN ESCs are high-end ESCs that allow control and feedback using a custom CAN protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:11
#: 9b2a65bdc56a4eccb7e571743b717e71
msgid "KDE has released new firmware that offers the option of using standard DroneCAN protocol or their custom CAN protocol. The following page details setup using older firmware or newer firmware when the custom CAN protocol is selected. To setup for use as a standard DroneCAN ESC see the firmware update and setup instructions `here <https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0496/8205/files/DroneCAN_QuickStart_1.0.3.pdf>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:13
#: 57ec01b247ce490ab68c966ee9154f35
msgid "Support for these ESCs in autopilots with less than 2MB flash is not included in standard firmware builds, but may be included by building firmware with KDE CAN support using the `custom firmware build server <https://custom.ardupilot.org>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:16
#: 0665f4e45e51443292e49c22e246c681
msgid "Where To Buy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:18
#: 88ab8bc03c954be3bfebafc225721ccb
msgid "`KDE-UAS125UVC-HE <https://www.kdedirect.com/collections/uas-multi-rotor-electronics/products/kde-uas125uvc-he>`__ and `KDE-UAS85UVC <https://www.kdedirect.com/collections/uas-multi-rotor-electronics/products/kde-uas85uvc>`__ can be purchased from `KDEDirect.com <https://www.kdedirect.com/collections/uas-multi-rotor-electronics>`__ (other KDE ESCs may also support CAN, check the images of the ESC, those with \"CAN\" written on the side should work)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:19
#: 5de38987682b4f3d966955af81bd1a40
msgid "`KDECAN Wire Kit <https://www.kdedirect.com/collections/kdecan-bus-cables/products/kdecan-kit-jst-ghr-wire-kit>`__ is also required"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:22
#: d7c3cad8e8194d4cbe4dd8c4c89d7515
msgid "Configuring the ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:24
#: f371f163f94a44059619a9aa39d59b4b
msgid "`KDE's instructions for connecting and configuring with ArduPilot are here <https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0496/8205/files/KDECAN_Pixhawk_QuickStart.pdf>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:26
#: e1fcec6f041842cea4418c57b4700d45
msgid "Download, install and run the `KDE Direct Device Manager <https://www.kdedirect.com/collections/uas-multi-rotor-electronics/products/kde-dms?page=specs>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:27
#: 2ae474684f794e18810599792094ced6
msgid "Connect the first ESC to your PC with a USB cable and configure the device as shown below"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:33
#: 9b994dae53b1487b92f913fba154d4b1
msgid "Repeat the configuration of all other ESCs increasing the \"KDECAN ESC ID\" by one each time.  It is best to label the ESC with a number that is the ESC ID - 1. Somewhat confusingly the lowest ESC IDs is 02 but this will mirror the autopilot's SERVO1 output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:36
#: 92f6162620aa48e2860a19d6e8e95ee4
msgid "Connecting the ESCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:38
#: a58092922deb497d83ad54db616a8bba
msgid "The 4-pin cable connecting the first ESC to the autopilot's CAN1 port must have all pins swapped on one end (ideally on the end connecting to the first ESC).  Pin1 (red) should be swapped with Pin4.  Pin2 should be swapped with Pin3.  This modified cable should be used to connect the autopilot's CAN1 port to the first ESC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:39
#: 0facecc58af0405d834dcc25d77419c8
msgid "The ESCs should be daisy chained together using the KDECAN Wire Kit.  The CAN terminator (the 4-pin connector with a black loop) should be connected to the last ESC in the chain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:47
#: 319ca13648b949a79fefad446c8af23c
msgid "If using a CubeBlack autopilot, the CAN1 and CAN2 labels are reversed.  These instructions assume the ESCs are connected to the CAN1 port which is labelled \"CAN2\" on CubeBlack autopilots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:50
#: 749fcca78ac34cb1ba7ff16f53f0be66
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:52
#: 6e6fd2e65ebd4d9cae200ce24313728e
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_D1_PROTOCOL <CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` = 8 (KDECAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:53
#: 3123e01f05184200bc8168ac7bc3ffb1
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_P1_DRIVER <CAN_P1_DRIVER>` = 1 (First driver) to specify that the ESCs are connected to the CAN1 port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:54
#: f3309616107247b7b2ac3303b7d4436e
msgid "Set :ref:`MOT_PWM_MIN <MOT_PWM_MIN>` = 1000 and :ref:`MOT_PWM_MAX <MOT_PWM_MAX>` = 2000 so ArduPilot uses an output range that matches the ESCs input range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:55
#: 3e98acc1ac5842ea9e52602afda7a2bb
msgid "Set :ref:`KDE_NPOLE <KDE_NPOLE>` to the number of poles on the motor (Note it may be necessary to reboot the autopilot to cause this parameter to appear).  If you are not sure of the number, you can probably count them by looking closely into the top of the motor.  Even if set incorrectly the motors should spin normally because this number is only used to calculate the RPM reported to the ground station and stored in the onboard logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:58
#: 2f864bcf56e64c79ab4a479c65f2f8a7
msgid "Logging and Reporting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:60
#: e776a7af9f3449e086ed9932ec2ce9a2
msgid "KDECAN ESCs provide information back to the autopilot which is recorded in the autopilot's onboard log's ESCn messages and can be viewed in any :ref:`ArduPilot compatible log viewer <common-logs>`.  This information includes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:62
#: 7e01d0c9e9004550b91d317ea66c6630
msgid "RPM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:63
#: 9beee5591e3c412292b3e1549ea65476
msgid "Voltage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:64
#: 80706793596744009a585d7b24070604
msgid "Current"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:65
#: 95e1fd3bf59440eebfd8601a1f55202e
msgid "ESC Temperature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:66
#: 875f06d66da64cc38845b968a3d89e17
msgid "Total Current"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:68
#: 071056f589f04a9d865497a65e6e4d3f
msgid "The RCOU messages are also written to the onboard logs which hold the requested output level sent to the ESCs expressed as a number from 1000 (meaning stopped) to 2000 (meaning full output)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:70
#: e7e60dcf86ba42a6ac9bef503eb84126
msgid "This information can also be viewed in real-time using a ground station.  If using the Mission Planner go to the Flight Data screen's status tab and look for esc1_rpm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kde-can-escs.rst:78
#: 0416347dee0f42e5a1f47351db4d2ad3
msgid "Sending ESC data to the GCS requires using MAVLink2.  Please check the appropriate SERIALx_PROTOCOL parameter is 2 (where \"x\" is the serial port number used for the telemetry connection)."
msgstr ""
